  "notes": "The most song-oriented harmonic writer on this bench, and the model says so where it matters: real functional harmony with guitar-voiced I–V–vi–IV beside i–VI–III–VII, `borrowed.V` at 0.25 for the pre-chorus lifts, `chordToneBias` 0.82 and an arch-weighted contour because the hooks are written to be sung. The rhythm section is the crossover one — `snare.fullTimeVariantProb` 0.4 puts a straight 2&4 backbeat under nearly half the seeds, `rimshotLayer` is on, tambourine and shaker sit on the perc lanes, and `humanize.quantizeStrength` drops to 0.85 for the live-kit feel. The bass is `independent_riff` with authored cell shapes because the research says the 808 doubles a guitar-derived bass line, or is replaced outright by a real bass. ⚠ The research gives two poles (70–95 straight on the crossover cuts, 130–150 half-time on the trap ones). This model is the trap pole; `session.halfTime` is one flag, so the country-side tempo is carried by the harmony and the song form rather than by the clock. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 45 to 44 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 45 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
